{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread","id":1530919,"title":"The Black Hand or Tal'Mahe'Ra thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-15T12:46:28-08:00","id":1530919,"title":"The Black Hand or Tal'Mahe'Ra thread","content":"This is thread to discuss the Tal'Mah'Re and the Black Hand of DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND and the V20's THE BLACK HAND: GUIDE TO THE TAL'MAHE'RA with also nods towards the Orphans of Enoch from FORBIDDEN RELIGIONS.<br /> <br /> Basically, what do you love, hate, and in-between about them.<br /> <br /> Which was the best depiction of them and how should they be in modern games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T13:47:15-08:00","id":1530929,"title":"","content":"I thought the V20 guide struck a good balance with them as something you could build a campaign around (the writing in Dirty Secrets, whatever else can be said, I don't feel like it was completely there as a usable thing, if you will, so much as it threw a bunch of big insane ideas at you) without ignoring how gonzo they should be at heart (because if we're being honest, part of the allure of the True Hand is just how much it goes hard at being a trip to epic crazytown), but framing it with better writing. The V5 version is comparatively.. I don't really see the point, from my experience fans of the Tal'Mahe'Ra are entirely into how overwrought they are, and some toned down echo thing, it hits my &quot;who is this even for?&quot; buttons. People deeply into the True Hand aren't going to be happy with it, and people who feel validated by V5's general style of redoing things would likely have been just as happy if it were never mentioned at all again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I say that as someone who initially hated the True Hand, felt what was in retrospect petty vindictive glee at them being nuked in revised, and ultimately came around to &quot;you can just easily ignore them if you don't like them, it's not hurting anyone/the game if they exist and their fans are having fun, they don't need to be reduced to some pathetic echo to validate fanwars and authorial disdain&quot;. Not quite full on &quot;how I learned to stop worrying and love the True Black Hand&quot;, but, somewhere adjacent.<br /> <br /> I did generally like the True Brujah as an *idea*, with all that said, the concept of them, if not 100% the execution. The whole living relics channeling the power of their own decayed temporal stasis thing. Also you can go full bore &quot;The Timelord Victorious&quot; egomania/moral fall in a way that feels like it has some VtM resonance. I played one in a 7 year+ irl elder game and all, had a good time with exploring their thematics and historical angsts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T14:15:10-08:00","id":1530930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530929#post1530929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the V20 guide struck a good balance with them as something you could build a campaign around (the writing in Dirty Secrets, whatever else can be said, I don't feel like it was completely there as a usable thing, if you will, so much as it threw a bunch of big insane ideas at you) without ignoring how gonzo they should be at heart (because if we're being honest, part of the allure of the True Hand is just how much it goes hard at being a trip to epic crazytown), but framing it with better writing. The V5 version is comparatively.. I don't really see the point, from my experience fans of the Tal'Mahe'Ra are entirely into how overwrought they are, and some toned down echo thing, it hits my &quot;who is this even for?&quot; buttons. People deeply into the True Hand aren't going to be happy with it, and people who feel validated by V5's general style of redoing things would likely have been just as happy if it were never mentioned at all again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I say that as someone who initially hated the True Hand, felt what was in retrospect petty vindictive glee at them being nuked in revised, and ultimately came around to &quot;you can just easily ignore them if you don't like them, it's not hurting anyone/the game if they exist and their fans are having fun, they don't need to be reduced to some pathetic echo to validate fanwars and authorial disdain&quot;. Not quite full on &quot;how I learned to stop worrying and love the True Black Hand&quot;, but, somewhere adjacent.<br /> <br /> I did generally like the True Brujah as an *idea*, with all that said, the concept of them, if not 100% the execution. The whole living relics channeling the power of their own decayed temporal stasis thing. Also you can go full bore &quot;The Timelord Victorious&quot; egomania/moral fall in a way that feels like it has some VtM resonance. I played one in a 7 year+ irl elder game and all, had a good time with exploring their thematics and historical angsts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for sharing this insight!<br /> <br /> My own take on the subject is that I feel that the Tal'Mahe'Ra works perfectly fine in Vampire: The Masquerade but it's presented with 20% &quot;too much&quot; in Dirty Secrtes of the Black Hand. This is a very different percentage than fans who act like it's 200% too much or even 2000% too much. There's a lot of great ideas, many of which were incorporated into other parts of the setting but they all seem to run together when they're one.<br /> <br /> <b>Dirty Secrets</b><br /> <br /> <u>The Good</u><br /> <br /> * The Black Hand as a secret playing both sides against one another. It's vampire, conspiracies matter.<br /> * The existence of Revenant Families.<br /> * Worshipers of the Antediluvians.<br /> * Chatterlings as a concept are profoundly creepy.<br /> * The Old Clan Tzimisce<br /> * The description of Enoch.<br /> <br /> <u>The Bad</u><br /> <br /> * Enoch as a physical place you can visit in the Underworld.<br /> * Making it so that there's ANOTHER clan of mages that have seized undeath in the Nagaraja.<br /> * The Souleater concept feels out of step with the themes of V:TM and more werewolf.<br /> * The Black Hand are a bunch of inhuman, Antediluvian worshiping, Path walking, child kidnapping, manipulative Elders...and they are treated as &quot;the good guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, I feel the Black Hand is fine and about 1000x more interesting than what they did with the Inconnu in LAIR OF THE HIDDEN. One of the oldest and most interesting sects in V:TM ended up being a bunch of Elders living in a castle doing a regular Fawlty Towers plot. The Black Hand at least have some dignity and I kind of wish this was the write-up for the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> <b>The Nuking</b><br /> <br /> I think the nuking is pretty much embellic of the absolute worst elements of Revised because it's symbolic of just how utterly lacking in self-awareness 3rd Edition could be at time and how utterly arbitrary it was in its disdain. Basically, Revised treats the Black Hand as some sort of over-the-top ridiculous embarrassment before dropping a Nuke on the Underworld and having an Antediluvian kill 3,000,000 people in India with no one noticing. Oh and having nukes dropped on that Antediluvian along with a space laser.<br /> <br /> It acted above the silliness when it was silly itself.<br /> <br /> Pretty much like the Dark Age of Comics when so many superheroes had guns and black outfit while pretending that was somehow more mature than Superman or Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> <b>V20 Black Hand</b><br /> <br /> I mean there's very little to say here other than, &quot;the people at Onyx Path Publishing seem to have generally agreed with my above complaints.&quot; The version presented in V20 is toned down just enough that it fits the themes of V:TM a lot more. Linking the Tal'Mahe'Ra to the <b>Servitors of Irad</b> and other existing Gehenna Cults more or less helps cement the idea that they're definitely potent movers and shakers in Camarilla society but they're not all powerful either.<br /> <br /> V20's Black Hand also seems to have writers much more aware that antediluvian worshiping Gehenna cult is POSSIBLY a bunch of bad guys. I will say that having the BAALI join them and be accepted was a bit much for me and I wonder if it was genius or over the top for suggesting the Tal'Mahe'Re were idiots that were in way over their heads trying to control the Jyhad from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> It also convinced me the Aralu were the Baali founders even if that doesn't quite much sense.<br /> <br /> <b>Orphans of Enoch</b><br /> <br /> The Orphans of Enoch are a group that I'm mostly okay with even if I don't see how I'd use them in a game versus the &quot;classic&quot; Tal'Mahe'Re. I like them because they're an attempt by OPP to keep fitting in as much of the old lore as possible when V5 is full of writers who like to pretend it is is a *hock spit* reboot. The fact that they portrayed the after effects of something as goofy and ludicrous as the spirit nuke as deeply traumatizing and serious is sosmething I have mad respect for.<br /> <br /> The Orphans aren't the Black Hand but they can rebuild them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-15-2024, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T18:39:26-08:00","id":1530939,"title":"","content":"Last year, I tried my hand at actually reading <b>Dirty Secrets</b>. Didn't get through the whole thing before my attention drifted elsewhere. But my assessment was that it was trying to work with some pretty neat ideas, that ultimately came to the table half baked. Not to mention the book itself was half baked. It kind of bounces around with seemingly no rhyme or reason. It takes multiple chapters before the book drops the bombshell that it thinks the Tal'Mahe'Ra are &quot;the good guys&quot;. (Oh, and that there are spiritual parasites infesting the world. That bombshell too).<br /> <br /> While we're on the subject of the Souleaters, I see what <b>Dirty Secrets</b> was going for. They wanted to create a new set of antagonists for True Black Hand members to fight, so it isn't all just manipulating other factions. The content would seem very thin, if the book only showed up with a single WoD faction to add to the proceedings, whose only function was to infiltrate and subvert other factions.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Souleaters aren't really their own antagonists. They're every other game line's antagonists roughly bolted together and given the weakest motivations. It didn't add anything to the World of Darkness. If anything, it detracted from the nuances of other game lines, especially Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The only way it would really function without ruining the other games would be to explicitly state that the &quot;Souleaters&quot; concept was the Tal'Mahe'Ra barking up the wrong tree. That they were aware of all sorts of distinct forces acting in the world, including Banes and Fomori, but made the error of assuming they were all part of the same otherwordly force. In essence, supernatural conspiracy theorists. Just knowledgeable enough to see the threats, clueless enough to make incorrect assumptions about what it meant. Which, combined with their general paranoia and obsession with other conspiracies, makes them think there are infiltrators into their own organization where none exist. (Or at least aren't nebulous &quot;spiritual infection&quot; working within their members).<br /> <br /> Which I think is how V20 sort of boiled Souleaters down to. It's a fringe belief some Old Clan Tzimisce have, to justify not using Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of glad VtM decided to ignore Souleaters as a concept after <b>Dirty Secrets</b>. Could it have been reworked into something with more meat, that didn't step on every other splat's toes? Probably. But given how (arguably) central to the True Black Hand it was, I understand why White Wolf dropped it. As stated above, once you take the Souleaters out, there's not a lot for the Tal'Mahe'Ra to really stand on as a faction. You'd need to reorder the faction from the ground up. I don't blame White Wolf for not bothering. (The disdain with which they destroyed them in Revised, though, I can kind of blame them for).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T19:15:25-08:00","id":1530942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530939#post1530939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated above, once you take the Souleaters out, there's not a lot for the Tal'Mahe'Ra to really stand on as a faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that seems to MASSIVELY overstate the important of Souleaters that seemed a throwaway anatagonist faction for the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;Gehenna cult of antediluvian worshipers that has infiltrated both sects&quot; isn't interesting on its own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T19:50:38-08:00","id":1530944,"title":"","content":"I was one of those people who hated Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand when it first came out, but my opinion has since shifted. It was a long time before I actually ever read Dirty Secrets, as it was an incredibly rare supplement to find from my experience. So everything I knew about it was secondhand. However, the multiplicity of new bloodlines, strange Disciplines like Temporis, and many gonzo sounding ideas seemed like everything I didn't like about Vampire and not much that I did. Even when I did find a copy and read it, I still didn't like it though I was more impressed by what was actually written compared to how it was described to me. It's since grown on me.<br /> <br /> I do like some things about the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I like they are the next level of the Jyhad above the sects of the Camarilla and Sabbat. They are higher players in the Jyhad. There are other groups that I also place in this category - the Inconnu, the Children of Osiris, some of the Gehenna cults, some secret societies within each of the clans, and certain alliances of Methusalehs. They have very specific goals, have ancient and powerful vampires leading them, and they know deeper mysteries than other vampires. They are the string pullers that manipulate the sects below them. I think &quot;layering&quot; the Jyhad like this is important in concept, even if in practical terms it does not affect routine game play. There is probably another layer between them and the Antedeluvians, but this is probably the last practical level of higher Jyhad you can get to in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> I do like certain payoffs from earlier Easter eggs. The Brujah clanbook first introduced the concept of the True Brujah. Here they are actually shown. Viccisitude was clearly inspired by Necroscope vampires so the Souleaters completed that concept. It explains the origins of the Revenants. It shows the Sabbat is just as badly manipulated by ancient vampires as the Camarilla is.<br /> <br /> I also think it's the first sourcebook to introduce the Bahari and Lilith as an alternate figure for the &quot;true&quot; origin of vampirism. That's probably has been the most successful thing in it.<br /> <br /> I also like the fact that the game had these deeper mysteries and secrets. The problem was that by publishing them, they were no longer secrets. Every gormless jackass who had the book now knew all this stuff, rendering their use as mysteries in your chronicle moot. I did a lot of eye rolling every time someone used their metagame knowledge to &quot;solve&quot; or &quot;guess&quot; things IC in a chronicle that they could never have done if this book was not published. So instead of using this stuff outright as written, I now like to think of DSotBH as more of a showcase of the kind of mysteries you should be creating for your own version of the setting. I keep some things that were introduced in this sourcebook, change others, and ignore anything I don't like.<br /> <br /> Once I stopped treating it like &quot;canon&quot; I had to use in my chronicle, and saw it more like a toolbox I could use to build my own chronicle setting, I became a fan. It's better as a supplement for NPCs than using it to create PCs who are members of the sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chatterlings as a concept are profoundly creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the chatterlings too. They provide great mood. Unfortunately I haven't been able to think of a good way to include them in my regular chronicles<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enoch as a physical place you can visit in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense given the &quot;physics&quot; of the World of Darkness. None of Enoch is of course &quot;physical&quot;. This is just the relic of the destroyed city in the underworld because that's what happens when things of significance get destroyed. I did find it odd that it's located in the Shadowlands (somewhere in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean) rather than being some island in the Tempest like Stygia or the other Dark Kingdoms. Because of its location in the Atlantic Ocean, I've always wondered if that was a clue that the antedeluvian world was in fact some version of Atlantis rather than a strictly Biblical version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Souleater concept feels out of step with the themes of V:TM and more werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just as &quot;vampire&quot; as vicissitude and lots of people love that for some reason. The two go together because the only reason either exists in Vampire is because of Necroscope. If you don't like Necroscope style vampires, ditch both. That is what I do in my chronicles. I give the Tzimisce Protean instead. I don't see any point in keeping vicissitude but ditching the soul eaters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Hand are a bunch of inhuman, Antediluvian worshiping, Path walking, child kidnapping, manipulative Elders...and they are treated as &quot;the good guys.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I find it hard to see how the True Black Hand see themselves as protectors of humanity given all the stuff they do. It's not adequately explained why the True Black Hand thinks the Antedeluvians want to protect mankind, or how they reconcile that with some of the terrible stuff they do. Sometimes you need to read a World of Darkness sourcebook critically because that's how the writers want you to do in order to figure out things. But sometimes things are just badly implemented. I have no problem with the True Black Hand being hypocrites, or that even in some ways they do somehow make the world &quot;better&quot; than it would be without them. But it just doesn't quite succeed at reconciling these poles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It acted above the silliness when it was silly itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Revised could be very sneering at concepts and players who had different tastes than the Developer. The example I used was how exactly armies of shambling Vozhd in the streets of a modern American city, yet somehow never endangering the Masquerade, was any less silly than the things they got rid of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T20:14:57-08:00","id":1530945,"title":"","content":"I agree with you it should be an island in the Tempest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530944#post1530944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just as &quot;vampire&quot; as vicissitude and lots of people love that for some reason. The two go together because the only reason either exists in Vampire is because of Necroscope. If you don't like Necroscope style vampires, ditch both. That is what I do in my chronicles. I give the Tzimisce Protean instead. I don't see any point in keeping vicissitude but ditching the soul eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I suppose it's a question of how you're defining Vicissitude. Vicissitude is a much more flexible discipline than Protean so having it so that Dracula can shapeshift between an old man, a handsome young aristocrate or something else is very different from becoming a wolf or bat rules wise. Also, Vicissitude as a kind of tool for giving vampires access to FrakensteinTM style plots is also pretty cool. Lots of vampire stories have vampires in control of some sort of deformed monster or creatures.<br /> <br /> You don't need, &quot;And this is an infection from the Tzimisce Antediluvian or alien spirits&quot; to like the use of the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530944#post1530944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I find it hard to see how the True Black Hand see themselves as protectors of humanity given all the stuff they do. It's not adequately explained why the True Black Hand thinks the Antedeluvians want to protect mankind, or how they reconcile that with some of the terrible stuff they do. Sometimes you need to read a World of Darkness sourcebook critically because that's how the writers want you to do in order to figure out things. But sometimes things are just badly implemented. I have no problem with the True Black Hand being hypocrites, or that even in some ways they do somehow make the world &quot;better&quot; than it would be without them. But it just doesn't quite succeed at reconciling these poles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I get it if you phrase it in the context of, &quot;We are the Brothers Keeper and natural rulers of Seth's children by God's decree!&quot; religious nonsense but the Black Hand is portrayed very differently from the Salubri or even some versions of VII from Chronicles that would have a more straightforward &quot;Team Humanity&quot; handling of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Revised could be very sneering at concepts and players who had different tastes than the Developer. The example I used was how exactly armies of shambling Vozhd in the streets of a modern American city, yet somehow never endangering the Masquerade, was any less silly than the things they got rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much my feelings 100%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T21:16:09-08:00","id":1530947,"title":"","content":"I don't necessarily love or hate the Soul Eaters, but when I used them, I changed them to be part of a hive mind formed by the Kupala. In its attempt to escape its prison, when it helped the Tzimisce anarchs break their blood blonds, the Kupala essentially infected the Discipline of Vicissitude. Most of the Kupala is still stuck in Transylvania, but it has slowly been moving its spiritual essence from its prison into the bodies of Kindred and other Vicissitude creatures. The Old Clan Tzimisce, who have a larger presence in the True Black Hand than they have in other sects, are largely aware of how Vicissitude has started to twist away from where it was in older nights, and have begun to push the True Black Hand to confront the threat, but they don't really know what's causing it and the True Black Hand has a lot on its plate, so Soul Eaters aren't really their main focus.<br /> <br /> In one game I ran the Kupala as the Eater of Souls, Soulof the Wyrm's triactic heads, imprisoned and trapped. <br /> <br /> In another game I ran the Kupala as one if the Children. Unlike the others, it was awake but couldn't break free from its bonds. It had its minions, the Baali line from the third Baali founder, the ones on the Path of the Hive. They would willingly join the Kupala's soul eater hivemind and practiced Vicissitude as an in-Clan discipline. <br /> <br /> In this case, Vicissitude was not an infection or corrupted, it was just this one sub-group using it in this way, it's just that the Old Clan hasn't realized it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-16-2024, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T22:31:37-08:00","id":1530950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530929#post1530929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the V20 guide struck a good balance with them as something you could build a campaign around (the writing in Dirty Secrets, whatever else can be said, I don't feel like it was completely there as a usable thing, if you will, so much as it threw a bunch of big insane ideas at you) without ignoring how gonzo they should be at heart (because if we're being honest, part of the allure of the True Hand is just how much it goes hard at being a trip to epic crazytown), but framing it with better writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have still likes to get much more hard facts about the goals, methods and the Antidiluvian Worship of the Black Hand (I mean there isn't even a Path of Enlightenment for that) and a map and more detalied description of Enoch.<br /> <br /> And I still don't get why they instead devoted an entire chapter of the book to the Bahari, that don't feel like their belives even align with what the goals of the sect are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T23:59:49-08:00","id":1530952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530950#post1530950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have still likes to get much more hard facts about the goals, methods and the Antidiluvian Worship of the Black Hand (I mean there isn't even a Path of Enlightenment for that) and a map and more detalied description of Enoch.<br /> <br /> And I still don't get why they instead devoted an entire chapter of the book to the Bahari, that don't feel like their belives even align with what the goals of the sect are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say the Guide was perfect, just that it was more usable for an actual campaign framework.<br /> <br /> With that said, I don't think you really need a path of enlightenment for every religious devotion, as opposed to that you can filter your existing path/road/morality through such wider religious faith as you have. You can believe in a lot of things/forces (and people do), even on humanity. Someone like Moncada was on power and inner voice and was nevertheless Turbo Catholic, for instance. In the DA setting, various Cainites on Road of Kings still believed in Christianity, so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 02-16-2024, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T00:39:35-08:00","id":1530954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530952#post1530952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said, I don't think you really need a path of enlightenment for every religious devotion,</div> </div> </div> </div>But the system usually provides path for religions, and even if a path isn't really needed the book still doesn't really give you a good description of their believes (making it even weirder that the Bahari got an entire chapter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T01:15:55-08:00","id":1530958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530954#post1530954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the system usually provides path for religions, and even if a path isn't really needed the book still doesn't really give you a good description of their believes (making it even weirder that the Bahari got an entire chapter).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the roads that especially cleaved to Christianity or Islam distinctly mostly puttered out in the modern era and were largely then as faiths the province of people on humanity. The system provides a path for religions sometimes, and other times goes &quot;you can still believe in this thing without one&quot;. Honestly, even the Assamite schism was helped along by that there were Muslim followers of the Path of Blood who were now plunged into a crisis of one being demanded over the other by the tiny apocalyptic horror monster in Alamut, as opposed to previously not having to do that.<br /> <br /> The other problem that I would say the True Hand somewhat makes for itself conceptually is that as the Antediluvians affiliated to it are kept as unknown figures with a generalized overname and their specific nature in dispute even amongst the Hand, is that coming up with a detailed set of practices for devotees would challenge even better writers.<br /> <br /> The Bahari thing was from my own read mostly that they were trying to push it as now a relevant part of the Hand/imply it had been so now *handwave* the whole time in some way or another (see Izhim's reaction to Lilin things), which, eh, your mileage certainly may vary on that move. I was pretty neutral on it. I think it was an effort to do something relevant with the Bahari beyond &quot;they're just kind of there&quot;, by tying them to a major faction, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T01:47:14-08:00","id":1530961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530958#post1530958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other problem that I would say the True Hand somewhat makes for itself conceptually is that as the Antediluvians affiliated to it are kept as unknown figures with a generalized overname and their specific nature in dispute even amongst the Hand, is that coming up with a detailed set of practices for devotees would challenge even better writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have been allready been happy with a short overlook about their core ethics, believes and goals (that I don't have dig out of some bloated fluff text).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530958#post1530958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bahari thing was from my own read mostly that they were trying to push it as now a relevant part of the Hand/imply it had been so now *handwave* the whole time in some way or another (see Izhim's reaction to Lilin things), which, eh, your mileage certainly may vary on that move. I was pretty neutral on it. I think it was an effort to do something relevant with the Bahari beyond &quot;they're just kind of there&quot;, by tying them to a major faction, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't have problem with the Bahari, I just find it odd that they get that much more space than any other faction, even if they seem to be pretty far what is the mainstream in the sect (and the mainstream seems just really underdeveloped).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T07:29:09-08:00","id":1530978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530954#post1530954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the system usually provides path for religions, and even if a path isn't really needed the book still doesn't really give you a good description of their believes (making it even weirder that the Bahari got an entire chapter).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to completely agree with this.<br /> <br /> The Tal'Mahe'Ra is supposed to be the biggest Gehenna cult, the oldest group of Antediluvian worshippers. Yet we got precious little information on the religious side of them. They're supposed to be a giant, fanatical religious cult, but I don't feel either of the Black Hand books presented them as a fanatical cult. I also agree I found it was strange to see the most in-depth look at the Bahari in the Black Hand book. Don't get me wrong, I really like the Bahari and it was nice to see them finally get some expansion, but I would have much preferred to see the Bahari get their own book, and for that chapter to have focused on the Tal'Mmahe'Ra's religious proclivities rather than that of the Bahari, who don't really have a place in the True Black Hand to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T08:58:03-08:00","id":1530980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530978#post1530978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to completely agree with this.<br /> <br /> The Tal'Mahe'Ra is supposed to be the biggest Gehenna cult, the oldest group of Antediluvian worshippers. Yet we got precious little information on the religious side of them. They're supposed to be a giant, fanatical religious cult, but I don't feel either of the Black Hand books presented them as a fanatical cult. I also agree I found it was strange to see the most in-depth look at the Bahari in the Black Hand book. Don't get me wrong, I really like the Bahari and it was nice to see them finally get some expansion, but I would have much preferred to see the Bahari get their own book, and for that chapter to have focused on the Tal'Mmahe'Ra's religious proclivities rather than that of the Bahari, who don't really have a place in the True Black Hand to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I should note the Bahari got their start in DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND with the Path of Lilith so it's not them being retconned as being part of the sect. It's the fact that the Black Hand is probably the biggest group of Lilith worshipers that exists circa 2nd Edition and possibly one of the few groups out there that has access to copies of THE REVELATIONS OF THE DARK MOTHER.<br /> <br /> This isn't something that necessarily contradicts their whole thing either as the Black Hand don't have the contradiction to Sabbat do. The Sabbat worship CAINE who hates Lilith and the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> The Tal'Mahe'Ra worship THE ANTEDILUVIANS which means that it doesn't matter if Caine or Lilith is the first vampire. They might even think it works better for their religion as Caine cursed the Thirteen while Lilith might have been all for them (if they ever met).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-16-2024, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T09:24:04-08:00","id":1530982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530930#post1530930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * The Souleater concept feels out of step with the themes of V:TM and more werewolf.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Tzimisce and the Shadow Lords had an intertwined history, back and forth explored in DA books, VTM books and Werewolf books, so in a strange yet fitting way the Souleaters for that age/edition mindset with the echoes of the lingering crossover &quot;friendliness&quot; of the early editions were quite understandable and... logical<br /> I mean the Gangrel could have been easily tied to the Wyld in similar way, even have Protean as a Wyld infection not unlike of the Black Furries' Metamorphic Plague or link the Brujah via their weakness to Frenzy to the Beast-of-War, but no other clans really had a presence so emphasized than the Tzimisce<br /> It was an interesting angle and personally I think The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra gave us a nice &quot;compromise&quot; in the form of the Path of Asakku (with a neat little link/possibility to Aretstikapha and the whole Qlippoth concept a neat Lovecraftian style)<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T09:45:27-08:00","id":1530984,"title":"","content":"I admit I actually note that A LOT of Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand filtered out from the Black Hand to the rest of the line and it doesn't get any credit for it:<br /> <br /> * The Bahari and Path of Lilith<br /> * The True Brujah<br /> * The Soul Eaters actually became the main focus of Revised's handling of the Tzimisce Antiediluvian and his Gehenna scenario. Except instead of Vicissitude being Banes infiltrating people, it was the means for the Eldest to infect people.<br /> * The Old Clan Tzimisce<br /> * The Nagaraja<br /> * Revenant Families<br /> <br /> It seems like a pretty large chunk of the book became pretty important to the metaplot and backstory of the game in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T10:50:08-08:00","id":1530990,"title":"","content":"Thanks for posting about this everyone! Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand is one of my favorite books, and I fought pretty hard on the old old forums for some proper discussion about the book, Back in the day you'd get instantly flamed at the mere mention of it... but I fought against that. So, I'm really glad to see it being discussed again... and civilly.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T11:43:52-08:00","id":1530994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530944#post1530944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So instead of using this stuff outright as written, I now like to think of DSotBH as more of a showcase of the kind of mysteries you should be creating for your own version of the setting. I keep some things that were introduced in this sourcebook, change others, and ignore anything I don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530984#post1530984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I actually note that A LOT of Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand filtered out from the Black Hand to the rest of the line and it doesn't get any credit for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was also my experience and that of friends. When the book came out, the general attitude was it was too gonzo and a resource for munchkins. Yet, everybody seemed to like <i>some</i> idea in it. In retrospect it feels like an overflow book with concepts omitted from various earlier books that were tied together with a narrative for the sake of publication, and they bundled up some things that didn't really fit with others. So cherry-picking and re-contextualizing was what most did with it.<br /> That so many of the ideas work on their own tells me that they are generally good ideas, and the problem was more with the presentation. I think the biggest points of conflict for most were the Souleaters and the overpowered Temporis together with the over-the-top setting. Having so much crammed into a single book also limited the space for development and background of the ideas, which may actually have been a good thing for when they got developed in later books.<br /> <br /> I generally like the V20 version as they tried to make the hodgepodge assembly somewhat more coherent, but it ultimately suffers from the same problem that so many of the things feel weirdly out of place when put into a single pot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T12:31:38-08:00","id":1530999,"title":"","content":"I'm a little late to the party on this thread, but here goes. I viewed Dirty Secrets of The Black Hand as a flawed mess that had an interesting idea behind it with a sect made up of elders and ancients who are manipulating the Sabbat and Camarilla for there own goals to serve what they think is the antidulivans will. But the setup was subpar and some of the ideas were not that great if I go by all the comments from old reviews of the sourcebook.<br /> <br /> What I liked were the sect believing they were serving the will of the 3rd generation and how they would play off the two sects off of each other and you could play potent elders if you wished and they had creation rules for that. I found the idea of Chatterlings interesting and creepy about young men and women being raised since childhood to become Kindred at early adult hood and would make even the most jaded kindred take a step back and might even feel sorry that these folks were denied a normal childhood and showed how even more inhuman these beings were.<br /> <br /> I liked the Old Clan Tzismce and Nagaraja lineages and what they brought to the table and I liked some of the new revenant families they created.<br /> <br /> What I didn't like was the Soul Eaters subplot being the source of the Fiends signature discipline and the introduction of the True Brujah bloodline with there signature power. I could get behind a line of Brujah that would lose there emotions over time as their founder was very cold in the beginging before whatever breakdown he had to create two distinct lineages. I could accept a line that lost there emotions, but I couldn\u2019t get behind Temporis as it fit better in a Mage or Changeling settings.<br /> <br /> I know that this sect saw themselves as &quot;good&quot; guys but you knew and saw right away it was a falsehood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-21-2024, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T14:44:41-08:00","id":1531006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530999#post1530999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that this sect saw themselves as &quot;good&quot; guys but you knew and saw right away it was a falsehood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was always glad that stuff like the Chatterlings were fairly prominent, because it made it clear that despite their protests, they were definitely monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T14:47:02-08:00","id":1531007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531006#post1531006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was always glad that stuff like the Chatterlings were fairly prominent, because it made it clear that despite their protests, they were definitely monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think THAT is why the Shadow Crusade feels so ludicrous and out of place.<br /> <br /> Becuase it justifies the Black Hand's claims of being monsters who fight monsters.<br /> <br /> Even though their origin story is the Black Hand brought them to Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T07:11:25-08:00","id":1531057,"title":"","content":"I unironically liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and I unironically believe that not only did it have the best depiction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra but that it is also superior to every single V5 book ever written. <br /> <br /> There, I said it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T09:49:24-08:00","id":1531060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531057#post1531057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I unironically liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and I unironically believe that not only did it have the best depiction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra but that it is also superior to every single V5 book ever written.<br /> <br /> There, I said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, Chicago by Night 5E is too awesome to be defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T12:10:48-08:00","id":1531066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531060#post1531060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, Chicago by Night 5E is too awesome to be defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I respectfully disagree.<br /> <br /> I think CbN 5E can't hold a candle to the OG CbN from 1991. I will concede that I think V5 Chicago is the least shitty of a very shitty lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T12:31:22-08:00","id":1531067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531066#post1531066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, I respectfully disagree.<br /> <br /> I think CbN 5E can't hold a candle to the OG CbN from 1991. I will concede that I think V5 Chicago is the least shitty of a very shitty lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on V5 can be summarized as I love OPP's V5 books and think considerably less of most others.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BUT do to the fact there's so many Kickstarter bonus books, there's a LOT of really good V5 books by OPP.<br /> <br /> I also like a lot of the spin off material like LA by Night, Seattle by Night, the Choice of Game text games, and the visual novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-18-2024, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T05:34:53-08:00","id":1531106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531057#post1531057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I unironically liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and I unironically believe that not only did it have the best depiction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra but that it is also superior to every single V5 book ever written.<br /> <br /> There, I said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know...I'm with you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T09:47:43-08:00","id":1531126,"title":"","content":"The one thing I never liked about the Tal'Mahe'Ra, besides (just like the Black Hand) the orientalism aspects of it, was that many times it's very confusing where the Hand Without a Sun commences and where the Black Hand ends. Like both using Seraph as a title makes everything weird. Having infiltrated members on the Black Hand, but hardly being clear how and when it is done deepens de confusion. <br /> <br /> Although I think the Inconnu end up being 'just a thing' and not a phenomena, not something that acts and moves, they manage to be surrounded by mystery, by an aura, some form of purpose. The TalMaheRa in my view never could be more than the 'I'm cooler than you cuz I'm from the secret faction inside the secret faction inside of the sect, inside the secret society of vampires'. Cuz not only is a hotpot of unique Bloodlines, but full of exclusive magics, wizards, mummies, and powers, and they have the OG vampire HQ just for baller more status.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the idea of a conspiracy that worships the Antes, and is as much of as paranoid fanatics as the Sabbat, but instead of destroying them they want to stand on their side, I think they are awesome. I love the idea of their struggle against the Lost Tribe for control of the Black Hand, although that basically is unexplored in the metaplot. Although that sometimes just muddles very heavily the Black Hand itself, and the Sabbat by an extension.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I like most, though, is cloaking them in as much of secret, conspiracy and esoteric mystery as possible. One of the most consistent eyes and hands of the Eternal Struggle, comparable to the Inconnu. With the very meta-understanding that they, in all their knowledge of Enoch and Noddism, still aren't 100% sure if the Antediluvians are all what their knowledge and legends relate them to be. They are like too-deep and invested to back down now, but it is still a big freaking gamble if all their work, their horrendous acts, their centuries-spanning plots, will bear fruit, or be hubris. <br /> It is very Personal Horror and Gothic for them to know not if their Gods exist, if they know Their design, or if they are of any relevancy to Their plans.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, they should be very few but apex in power and knowledge, and also have taken part in some of the most Darkness of the World of Darkness out of pure research, functionality and projects. To me they are a cooler, grimmer and material-oriented version of the inconnu, that want to escape from the Curse by being in the side of the Divinely Cursed, instead of wanting to escape it by forsaken and somehow surpassing the Curse spiritually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T11:13:54-08:00","id":1531129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531126#post1531126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I never liked about the Tal'Mahe'Ra, besides (just like the Black Hand) the orientalism aspects of it, was that many times it's very confusing where the Hand Without a Sun commences and where the Black Hand ends. Like both using Seraph as a title makes everything weird. Having infiltrated members on the Black Hand, but hardly being clear how and when it is done deepens de confusion.<br /> <br /> Although I think the Inconnu end up being 'just a thing' and not a phenomena, not something that acts and moves, they manage to be surrounded by mystery, by an aura, some form of purpose. The TalMaheRa in my view never could be more than the 'I'm cooler than you cuz I'm from the secret faction inside the secret faction inside of the sect, inside the secret society of vampires'. Cuz not only is a hotpot of unique Bloodlines, but full of exclusive magics, wizards, mummies, and powers, and they have the OG vampire HQ just for baller more status.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the idea of a conspiracy that worships the Antes, and is as much of as paranoid fanatics as the Sabbat, but instead of destroying them they want to stand on their side, I think they are awesome. I love the idea of their struggle against the Lost Tribe for control of the Black Hand, although that basically is unexplored in the metaplot. Although that sometimes just muddles very heavily the Black Hand itself, and the Sabbat by an extension.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I like most, though, is cloaking them in as much of secret, conspiracy and esoteric mystery as possible. One of the most consistent eyes and hands of the Eternal Struggle, comparable to the Inconnu. With the very meta-understanding that they, in all their knowledge of Enoch and Noddism, still aren't 100% sure if the Antediluvians are all what their knowledge and legends relate them to be. They are like too-deep and invested to back down now, but it is still a big freaking gamble if all their work, their horrendous acts, their centuries-spanning plots, will bear fruit, or be hubris.<br /> It is very Personal Horror and Gothic for them to know not if their Gods exist, if they know Their design, or if they are of any relevancy to Their plans.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, they should be very few but apex in power and knowledge, and also have taken part in some of the most Darkness of the World of Darkness out of pure research, functionality and projects. To me they are a cooler, grimmer and material-oriented version of the inconnu, that want to escape from the Curse by being in the side of the Divinely Cursed, instead of wanting to escape it by forsaken and somehow surpassing the Curse spiritually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Black Hand are full of THINGS and are plots and INTRIGUE and IDEAS.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu turned out to be 13 guys who live in the same apartment building debating religion for a thousand years because they all have a crush on Saulot.<br /> <br /> It's the biggest anticlimax for a mystery after Baba Yaga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T13:30:17-08:00","id":1531141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531129#post1531129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the Black Hand are full of THINGS and are plots and INTRIGUE and IDEAS.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu turned out to be 13 guys who live in the same apartment building debating religion for a thousand years because they all have a crush on Saulot.<br /> <br /> It's the biggest anticlimax for a mystery after Baba Yaga.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm with you on the Inconnu anticlimax, it doesn't even make much sense honestly. It's like a big brother elders show.<br /> But I was talking more like the organization and practice of the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Black Hand is full of those thing, which I like. I think it sounded like I was not liking most of what the TalMaheRa has, but that's not it, my bad.<br /> <br /> And Baba Yaga dying in a railroad spooky train ride to a #creepy_child_vampire who also just disappears, leaving the PCs holding the big nothing of having witnessed that, is a great comparison. XD<br /> <br /> Although I think the Lair of the Hidden is an interesting chronicle idea. It just came in sacrifice of a very important sect, Infernalism, and an Antediluvian (with no extra charge)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T11:54:43-08:00","id":1531239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531141#post1531141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm with you on the Inconnu anticlimax, it doesn't even make much sense honestly. It's like a big brother elders show.<br /> But I was talking more like the organization and practice of the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Black Hand is full of those thing, which I like. I think it sounded like I was not liking most of what the TalMaheRa has, but that's not it, my bad.<br /> <br /> And Baba Yaga dying in a railroad spooky train ride to a #creepy_child_vampire who also just disappears, leaving the PCs holding the big nothing of having witnessed that, is a great comparison. XD<br /> <br /> Although I think the Lair of the Hidden is an interesting chronicle idea. It just came in sacrifice of a very important sect, Infernalism, and an Antediluvian (with no extra charge)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Lair of the Hidden was a bit of a disappointment.<br /> <br /> I unironically vastly prefer the 1st Edition version of the Inconnu that were more or less the closest things to &quot;good guys&quot; alongside the Children of Osiris and the 1e Salubri. And those are all canon at my gaming table.<br /> <br /> I still have Hunedoara Castle as the HQ of the Inconnu in my games and I also included Drenis as a pathetic Cappadocian who tried to create Clan Hecata only to get wiped out by the Giovanni, but that's about it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T13:09:43-08:00","id":1531249,"title":"","content":"It's still possible to use the Inconnu as a sect that wants to transcend the weakness of their state by following all sorts of tests on themselves and others and many would be inhumane and culling feifdoms out of frustration if there experiments don't bear the results they hoped for or if they think that they maybe endangered themselves to the thirsty fangs of weaker kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T04:18:40-08:00","id":1531284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531006#post1531006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was always glad that stuff like the Chatterlings were fairly prominent, because it made it clear that despite their protests, they were definitely monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Years ago I ran a Tal'Mahe'Ra story where my modern day characters where recruited into the Hand, and when they saw what they were doing with the Chatterlings they were like WTF!? Ultimately they joined, but yea, the Tal'Mahe'Ra are certainly messed up, as much as I love em. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531129#post1531129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inconnu turned out to be 13 guys who live in the same apartment building debating religion for a thousand years because they all have a crush on Saulot.<br /> <br /> It's the biggest anticlimax for a mystery after Baba Yaga.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never did much with the Inconnu, but I always pictured them as at least a slightly larger, more organized group with a goal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Were I to do something with now, I'd definitely do something different than the canon version.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T07:35:14-08:00","id":1531292,"title":"","content":"I know it is a tangent, but I do think the TalMaheRa and the Inconnu as somewhat of opposite sides of the same coin of elder retirement, fear and terrified hopes, after all fails. <br /> <br /> But I've always found weird that the Inconnu HQ ins Huneodora is very close to Ceoris geographically, but most importantly that while they are in the middle of Kupala territory they made a weird pact with another demon... I don't know if the writers just didn't want to deal with Kupa cuz it might've be affected by the Transylvanian Chronicles, and so the writers preferred to make a separate demon as to keep the Lair of the Hidden independent from it... or if they had specifics that just didn't fit the bigger demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, back on track. Which Seraphs from the Black Hand were influenced (or even secret affiliate to) the TalMaheRa? This is something I never understood if was a thing, or if the TMR swayed the Sabbat more indirectly. <br /> Also, I wonder in which century the TMR took control of the Black Hand from the Lost Tribe, I think the story of Anosh, the first Seraph, tells it, but I don't remember. It was a very quiet takeover all things consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T09:45:44-08:00","id":1531296,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Izhim ur-Baal and Djuhah were Tal'Mahe'Ra, Jalan Ajav definitely was not, and Elimelech might or might not have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T12:23:44-08:00","id":1531303,"title":"","content":"If I go by Children Of The Night. Jalan and Elimelech were part of the Tal'Mahe'Ra and not many of them felt comfortable being alone with Elimelech in general as he could only feed from fellow Kindred and his derangements were wearing away what little humanity he had left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T13:11:05-08:00","id":1531306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1531303#post1531303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I go by Children Of The Night. Jalan and Elimelech were part of the Tal'Mahe'Ra and not many of them felt comfortable being alone with Elimelech in general as he could only feed from fellow Kindred and his derangements were wearing away what little humanity he had left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beckett's Jyhad Diary had Jalan actively trying to purge the Black Hand as part of the next Sabbat Civil War, forcing it out into the open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T14:03:06-08:00","id":1531308,"title":"","content":"That does sound like something that Jalan would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:28:32-08:00","id":1531352,"title":"","content":"I was never enough of an admirer of the Necroscope novels to find the Souleaters useful, but I've found the V20 volume's Path of Asakku a terrific Storyteller tool for getting into the head of an NPC vampire of *any* clan who has been hollowed out by their founder. It's a more useful tool for Gehenna stories than anything that appeared in the Gehenna book from 20 years ago. Swap out Vicissitude for whatever clan discipline you think best represents the clan founder as their vector for control over their progeny and you're good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 02-23-2024, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:04:00-07:00","id":1536949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530919-the-black-hand-or-tal-mahe-ra-thread?p=1530944#post1530944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was one of those people who hated Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand when it first came out, but my opinion has since shifted. It was a long time before I actually ever read Dirty Secrets, as it was an incredibly rare supplement to find from my experience. So everything I knew about it was secondhand. However, the multiplicity of new bloodlines, strange Disciplines like Temporis, and many gonzo sounding ideas seemed like everything I didn't like about Vampire and not much that I did. Even when I did find a copy and read it, I still didn't like it though I was more impressed by what was actually written compared to how it was described to me. It's since grown on me.<br /> <br /> I do like some things about the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I like they are the next level of the Jyhad above the sects of the Camarilla and Sabbat. They are higher players in the Jyhad. There are other groups that I also place in this category - the Inconnu, the Children of Osiris, some of the Gehenna cults, some secret societies within each of the clans, and certain alliances of Methusalehs. They have very specific goals, have ancient and powerful vampires leading them, and they know deeper mysteries than other vampires. They are the string pullers that manipulate the sects below them. I think &quot;layering&quot; the Jyhad like this is important in concept, even if in practical terms it does not affect routine game play. There is probably another layer between them and the Antedeluvians, but this is probably the last practical level of higher Jyhad you can get to in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> I do like certain payoffs from earlier Easter eggs. The Brujah clanbook first introduced the concept of the True Brujah. Here they are actually shown. Viccisitude was clearly inspired by Necroscope vampires so the Souleaters completed that concept. It explains the origins of the Revenants. It shows the Sabbat is just as badly manipulated by ancient vampires as the Camarilla is.<br /> <br /> I also think it's the first sourcebook to introduce the Bahari and Lilith as an alternate figure for the &quot;true&quot; origin of vampirism. That's probably has been the most successful thing in it.<br /> <br /> I also like the fact that the game had these deeper mysteries and secrets. The problem was that by publishing them, they were no longer secrets. Every gormless jackass who had the book now knew all this stuff, rendering their use as mysteries in your chronicle moot. I did a lot of eye rolling every time someone used their metagame knowledge to &quot;solve&quot; or &quot;guess&quot; things IC in a chronicle that they could never have done if this book was not published. So instead of using this stuff outright as written, I now like to think of DSotBH as more of a showcase of the kind of mysteries you should be creating for your own version of the setting. I keep some things that were introduced in this sourcebook, change others, and ignore anything I don't like.<br /> <br /> Once I stopped treating it like &quot;canon&quot; I had to use in my chronicle, and saw it more like a toolbox I could use to build my own chronicle setting, I became a fan. It's better as a supplement for NPCs than using it to create PCs who are members of the sect.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the chatterlings too. They provide great mood. Unfortunately I haven't been able to think of a good way to include them in my regular chronicles<br /> <br /> <br /> It makes sense given the &quot;physics&quot; of the World of Darkness. None of Enoch is of course &quot;physical&quot;. This is just the relic of the destroyed city in the underworld because that's what happens when things of significance get destroyed. I did find it odd that it's located in the Shadowlands (somewhere in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean) rather than being some island in the Tempest like Stygia or the other Dark Kingdoms. Because of its location in the Atlantic Ocean, I've always wondered if that was a clue that the antedeluvian world was in fact some version of Atlantis rather than a strictly Biblical version.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is just as &quot;vampire&quot; as vicissitude and lots of people love that for some reason. The two go together because the only reason either exists in Vampire is because of Necroscope. If you don't like Necroscope style vampires, ditch both. That is what I do in my chronicles. I give the Tzimisce Protean instead. I don't see any point in keeping vicissitude but ditching the soul eaters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree. I find it hard to see how the True Black Hand see themselves as protectors of humanity given all the stuff they do. It's not adequately explained why the True Black Hand thinks the Antedeluvians want to protect mankind, or how they reconcile that with some of the terrible stuff they do. Sometimes you need to read a World of Darkness sourcebook critically because that's how the writers want you to do in order to figure out things. But sometimes things are just badly implemented. I have no problem with the True Black Hand being hypocrites, or that even in some ways they do somehow make the world &quot;better&quot; than it would be without them. But it just doesn't quite succeed at reconciling these poles.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, Revised could be very sneering at concepts and players who had different tastes than the Developer. The example I used was how exactly armies of shambling Vozhd in the streets of a modern American city, yet somehow never endangering the Masquerade, was any less silly than the things they got rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree about the Tal-whatever being portrayed as good guys. Well, they weren't, and they weren't portrayed as truly evil, and depraved, which they were. This is the problem with the late 90's WW output. They smelled big money when VtM was more successful than they ever dreamed, and they pumped out metafiction like a crack addict. And they lost sight, or intentionally ignored, the &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect. We then got centuries old monsters who were &quot;Relatively Nice Guys&quot; after 2,000 years, like Critias. Which makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> You have Elimelech, who is politely and vaguely portrayed as &quot;Grandfatherly, but don't be alone with him. He's kid of creepy, and may ask you to sit on his lap, when you're 12.&quot; No, with Humanity 0, which should not be possible with WW's rules, he'll invite you to have some Chicken Tendies, then make you taste your own kidneys before you die. And laugh while doing it. The other members of the Ruling Council (I can't remember the name) won't be alone with him because he'll try to eat them, and he's strong enough to take any of them one on one. But hey, he's now pretending to be a mortal chatterling in Ghostenoch, and nobody remembers who he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}